<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Marcus Garvey</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1887">1887</a>–<a href="/years/1940">1940</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Marcus Garvey was a Jamaican political activist who founded the Universal Negro Improvement Association in 1914 and led a mass movement of black pride and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pan-africanism">Pan-Africanism</a>, based in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> from 1916. In the early 1920s his organisation negotiated to settle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/african-americans">African Americans</a> in Liberia, but the Liberian government turned against the plan. He was deported from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> in 1927.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/marcus-garvey.jpg" alt="Marcus Garvey" width="320" height="419" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Keystone View Company, restored by Creator:Adam Cuerden · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Marcus_Garvey,_%22Provisional_President_of_Africa%22,_by_the_Keystone_View_Company.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
